{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-de3886f9-dc03-4bf0-8439-3c5c91497f5e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b761004089115643","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9017-lz8ke5ny/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9017-E001.md","content":"# Keyboard accessibility remediation for the four audited Dashboard flows\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes the four audited core Dashboard flows — project creation,\nworkbench spawn, model deployment, and pipeline run submission — fully operable\nwith keyboard alone, and makes visible focus indicators consistent across\nthose flows. It resolves every defect enumerated in the accessibility audit\nreport for these flows: focus loss in modals, controls unreachable via\nkeyboard, and inconsistent focus indicators.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Remediate each defect enumerated in the accessibility audit report across\n  the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model deployment,\n  pipeline run submission):\n  - Fix focus handling in modals so focus is not lost — focus enters the modal\n    when it opens, remains trapped within it while it is open in the tab\n    order, and returns to the triggering control when it closes.\n  - Make every interactive control in the audited flows reachable and\n    operable via keyboard (tab order, arrow-key navigation where the control\n    type expects it, Enter/Space activation, Escape to dismiss).\n  - Apply a single consistent visible focus-indicator treatment across all\n    interactive controls in the audited flows, replacing the current\n    inconsistent indicator styles.\n- Out of scope per the strategy: screen-reader semantics beyond what the\n  keyboard fixes require, and any flows outside the four audited ones. Any\n  audited defect whose resolution would require out-of-scope semantics is\n  dispositioned with a recorded rationale rather than silently dropped.\n- The Dashboard's existing build pipeline and CI must remain green with these\n  changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model\n  deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end-to-end using the\n  keyboard alone, verified by a recorded keyboard-only walkthrough of each\n  flow.\n- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for these flows is resolved, or\n  explicitly dispositioned as out of scope with a recorded rationale.\n- No focus traps remain: opening and closing any modal in the audited flows\n  moves focus into the modal and returns it to the triggering control.\n- No unreachable controls remain: every interactive control in the audited\n  flows is reachable via keyboard and operable without a pointing device.\n- A single focus-indicator treatment is applied consistently across all\n  interactive controls in the audited flows (no per-page or per-flow indicator\n  variations).\n- The Dashboard's existing build pipeline is green with the changes included.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n  with no focus traps or unreachable controls.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n  flows.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":26989,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86f3f7ed4b58a65f","agent_id":"a3632a03eed2cbcf5","session_id":"c9c80b48-ecab-44d9-b48c-393a7058eb35","uuid":"7c10276e-1a5b-493d-a558-ab2ab6846c40","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:51:34.623Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9017 into epics"}
