able via keyboard (tab order, arrow-key navigation where the control\n50\t    type expects it, Enter/Space activation, Escape to dismiss).\n51\t  - Apply a single consistent visible focus-indicator treatment across all\n52\t    interactive controls in the audited flows, replacing the current\n53\t    inconsistent indicator styles.\n54\t- Out of scope per the strategy: screen-reader semantics beyond what the\n55\t  keyboard fixes require, and any flows outside the four audited ones. Any\n56\t  audited defect whose resolution would require out-of-scope semantics is\n57\t  dispositioned with a recorded rationale rather than silently dropped.\n58\t- The Dashboard's existing build pipeline and CI must remain green with these\n59\t  changes.\n60\t\n61\t## Acceptance Criteria\n62\t\n63\t- Each of the four audited flows (project creation, workbench spawn, model\n64\t  deployment, pipeline run submission) can be completed end-to-end using the\n65\t  keyboard alone, verified by a recorded keyboard-only walkthrough of each\n66\t  flow.\n67\t- Every defect enumerated in the audit report for these flows is resolved, or\n68\t  explicitly dispositioned as out of scope with a recorded rationale.\n69\t- No focus traps remain: opening and closing any modal in the audited flows\n70\t  moves focus into the modal and returns it to the triggering control.\n71\t- No unreachable controls remain: every interactive control in the audited\n72\t  flows is reachable via keyboard and operable without a pointing device.\n73\t- A single focus-indicator treatment is applied consistently across all\n74\t  interactive controls in the audited flows (no per-page or per-flow indicator\n75\t  variations).\n76\t- The Dashboard's existing build pipeline is green with the changes included.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: The four audited core flows are fully operable by keyboard,\n81\t  with no focus traps or unreachable controls.\n82\t- **HLR-2 (P1)**: Visible focus indicators are consistent across the audited\n83\t  flows.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b42bfd9f0fb05dd1","agent_id":"a8df4c9839dd94218","session_id":"c9c80b48-ecab-44d9-b48c-393a7058eb35","uuid":"4b6656eb-53aa-440c-81a7-27d4e8972b4e","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:53:47.835Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b95893e2d6663159","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9017 decomposition"}
